## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of demand paging, stack growth, race conditions, and memory protection at OS level; evaluates handling of concurrency and TLB effects.

## Key Concepts
- Guard pages and demand paging
- Atomic CAS for lock-free growth
- Per-thread stack limits and fairness
- Page table updates and TLB flush semantics

## Code Example
```c
// Pseudo-code: grow_stack(thread, fault_addr)
size_t new_base;
if (fault_addr < thread->stack_base - PAGE_SIZE) {
  if (atomic_cas(&thread->stack_base, fault_addr_base, fault_addr_base - PAGE_SIZE)) {
     page_t *p = allocate_page();
     map_page(thread->pid, new_base, p, PERM_READ_WRITE);
     flush_tlb(thread);
     return RESUME;
  } else {
     // another thread grew
     return retry_fault();
  }
}
```

